Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:04.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Can large language models combine skills they already know?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.01,0:00:13.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This COLM 2024 paper tests whether models solve an unseen composite task by fusing two simple tasks seen separately.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.87,0:00:17.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Across Llama and GPT, a sharp dichotomy emerges.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.84,0:00:21.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Suppose a model learned two simple tasks in-context,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.80,0:00:25.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}capitalizing certain words and swapping others.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.39,0:00:29.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Given an input needing both, can it combine the skills?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.58,0:00:34.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}For humans this is trivial, yet even GPT-4 and Claude 3 often fail.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.99,0:00:39.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Models are increasingly asked to chain skills for real reasoning,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.12,0:00:42.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}yet we lack a clear account of when chaining works.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.36,0:00:45.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Prior studies are narrow with little theory,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.16,0:00:48.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the failure reproduces easily on frontier models.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.83,0:00:55.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Three contributions: a test suite of linguistic and logical composite tasks with simple-task examples only;
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.87,0:01:00.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}evaluation across Llama and GPT scales revealing a clear dichotomy;
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.29,0:01:04.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and a linear self-attention theory explaining when composition emerges.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.26,0:01:08.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Two halves.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.71,0:01:12.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Empirically,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.16,0:01:15.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}each composite task is tested in four settings with ten in-context examples: each simple task alone,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.61,0:01:18.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a composite test with simple-task demos, and an all-composite gold standard.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.07,0:01:22.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Theoretically,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.52,0:01:25.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a linear self-attention model shows composition succeeds under confined support.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.27,0:01:28.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The suite pairs simple building blocks.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.06,0:01:32.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Linguistic tasks include capitalization, swapping,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.63,0:01:37.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and translations like phrase recombination and passive-to-active.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.27,0:01:41.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Logical tasks combine arithmetic with word operations.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.13,0:01:46.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Tasks split into separable composites, acting on different input parts,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.20,0:01:50.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and compose-by-step composites requiring chained reasoning.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.71,0:01:54.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A sharp split.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.55,0:01:58.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On separable composite tasks, models compose well and improve with scale,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.40,0:02:02.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}approaching the gold standard.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.24,0:02:06.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On compose-by-step tasks they collapse: Llama solves each simple task near ninety percent,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.09,0:02:09.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but the composite drops below twenty percent, and scaling doesn't help.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.23,0:02:12.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The scale sweep is the key ablation.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.87,0:02:16.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On separable tasks accuracy rises with scale;
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.16,0:02:19.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}on compose-by-step tasks it stays flat or degrades.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.89,0:02:24.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Swapping simple-task demos for composite ones recovers performance,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.80,0:02:28.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}isolating composition, not capability, as the bottleneck.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.27,0:02:30.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The numbers tell it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.74,0:02:35.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Simple capitalization and swap reach about ninety percent for Llama.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.73,0:02:40.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The compose-by-step version falls to twenty percent or lower,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.21,0:02:42.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with no gain from scaling.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.12,0:02:46.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Milder separable cases climb to forty-four and sixty-six percent.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.19,0:02:53.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The takeaway: models combine two skills only when they act on separate parts of the input.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.52,0:02:58.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}When a task needs genuinely chained, multi-step reasoning, they fail,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.38,0:03:00.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and more parameters won't help.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.56,0:03:03.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Task structure predicts whether scaling helps.
